From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] fix(memory): decide a write fault on physical memory
 under the lock it arrived with

Memory::AccessViolationCallback passed its lock to
PhysicalHeap::TriggerCallbacks, which releases it even when no watch
covers the page, and re-took the lock only afterwards for the host
protection check and the stale-protection recovery. When two threads
fault on the same watched page, the second finds the watch already
handled by the first. If a third thread re-armed the page in that gap
(EnablePhysicalMemoryAccessCallbacks, as a GPU cache does after
re-uploading it), the page was read-only again with its watch flag set,
and the recovery made it writable. EnableAccessCallbacks skips a page
whose flag is set, so the page was never protected again and its writes
went unreported for the rest of the run: a GPU copy of dynamic vertex
data in PGR4 went stale after hours of play, logged as "Recovered stale
physical page protection" for the same page.

The callback now checks the page's watch flag under the lock it was
called with, goes to TriggerCallbacks only for a watched page, and keeps
the lock through the protection check and the recovery, so no watch can
be armed in between. Xenia's MMIOHandler held one lock across its
protection check and the callback for the same reason.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---diff --git a/include/rex/system/xmemory.h b/include/rex/system/xmemory.h
--- a/include/rex/system/xmemory.h
+++ b/include/rex/system/xmemory.h
@@ -324,6 +324,9 @@ class PhysicalHeap : public BaseHeap {
   bool TriggerCallbacks(rex::thread::global_unique_lock_type global_lock_locked_once,
                         uint32_t virtual_address, uint32_t length, bool is_write,
                         bool unwatch_exact_range, bool unprotect = true);
+  // Whether the host page holding a guest address of this heap is write-watched.
+  // Callers must hold the global critical region.
+  bool IsWriteWatched(uint32_t virtual_address) const;
 
   uint32_t GetPhysicalAddress(uint32_t address) const;
 
diff --git a/src/system/xmemory.cpp b/src/system/xmemory.cpp
--- a/src/system/xmemory.cpp
+++ b/src/system/xmemory.cpp
@@ -616,14 +616,20 @@ bool Memory::AccessViolationCallback(rex::thread::global_unique_lock_type global
   //
   // Will be rounded to physical page boundaries internally, so just pass 1 as
   // the length - guranteed not to cross page boundaries also.
+  //
+  // The watch is checked here because TriggerCallbacks releases the lock even
+  // when it finds none, and the rest of the fault must be decided under the
+  // lock it arrived with. A watch another thread armed in between would leave
+  // the page read-only with its flag set, the recovery below would make it
+  // writable, and EnableAccessCallbacks, which skips a page whose flag is set,
+  // would never protect it again: its writes would go unreported for good.
   auto physical_heap = static_cast<PhysicalHeap*>(heap);
-  if (physical_heap->TriggerCallbacks(std::move(global_lock_locked_once), virtual_address, 1,
-                                      is_write, false)) {
-    return true;
+  if (is_write && physical_heap->IsWriteWatched(virtual_address)) {
+    return physical_heap->TriggerCallbacks(std::move(global_lock_locked_once), virtual_address, 1,
+                                           is_write, false);
   }
 
-  // No watch covers the page. TriggerCallbacks released the global lock.
-  auto global_lock = global_critical_region_.Acquire();
+  // No watch covers the page.
   if (HostPageAllowsAccess(host_address, is_write)) {
     return true;
   }
@@ -2418,6 +2424,14 @@ bool PhysicalHeap::IsHostPageWriteWatched(uint32_t host_page_number) const {
           (uint64_t(1) << (host_page_number & 63))) != 0;
 }
 
+bool PhysicalHeap::IsWriteWatched(uint32_t virtual_address) const {
+  if (virtual_address < heap_base_ || virtual_address - heap_base_ >= heap_size_) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  return IsHostPageWriteWatched((virtual_address - heap_base_ + host_address_offset()) /
+                                system_page_size_);
+}
+
 uint32_t PhysicalHeap::GetPhysicalAddress(uint32_t address) const {
   assert_true(address >= heap_base_);
   address -= heap_base_;
-- 
